      "role": "assistant",
      "content": "Be mindful that communication norms vary globally; directness valued in one culture might be perceived as aggression in another, while deference might be mistaken for a lack of conviction. Some cultural frameworks prioritize consensus-building through nuanced discussion over singular, immediate declaration of authority. Instead of \"polish,\" evaluate if their style aligns with the *specific* organizational culture the client operates within, recognizing diverse leadership styles are valid adaptations of strategic thought.",
